# Per-run artifacts of the alignment module.
# Every entry here is produced by a training run, not authored — see the file or
# script named alongside it. Committed inputs (o2sim_geometry.root,
# ITSAlignment.root, NetworkParameters/, UpdateSensorsList.txt, TrendingNetwork.tgz,
# YMLPBeamProfile.h, batch_train, profile_beam.log) are deliberately not listed.

# Training input, supplied per campaign and often a symlink to data kept outside
# the repository. YAlignment::SetSourceDataName in run_train_circle.C
XXXXinput.root

# Intermediate and analysis trees. YAlignment::PrepareData / AnalyzeMLP /
# ReconstructGeometries
XXXXtrain.root
XXXXanalyse.root
XXXXGeom.root
Geom/

# Step directories and their archives. run_train_circle.C renames MLPTrain to
# MLPTrain_Step<N>; process_all_train.sh tars it
MLPTrain/
MLPTrain_Step*/
MLPTrain_Step*.tgz

# Job log. process.sh redirects stdout here, process_all_train.sh renames it
train.log

# Monitoring dumps. YMultiLayerPerceptron::DumpResiduals / DumpCostGradients
Residual_Epoch_At_*.root
Residual_Monitor_Epoch_At_*.root
CostGradient_Epoch_At_*.txt
NTracksBySensor_Epoch*.txt

# Per-epoch weight snapshots written to the working directory before being moved
# into MLPTrain/weights/. YMultiLayerPerceptron::DumpWeights
weights_Epoch_At_*.txt
weightsDU_Epoch_At_*.txt

# Plots. Loss curve, per-sensor and per-half-stave track monitors, residual means
*.gif

# TrendingNetwork.tgz is tracked; the directory extracted from it at run time is not
TrendingNetwork/

# ACLiC build products and the MakeProject-generated AlignParam library, both
# regenerable: tools/make_alignlib.C and root -l 'tools/*.C+'
tools/AlignLib/
tools/*_C.so
tools/*_C.d
tools/*_C_ACLiC_dict_rdict.pcm

# Stray MakeProject output if a macro is run from the repository root
/AlignLib/

# Generated geometry cache. Regenerable in seconds from the committed geometry and
# alignment files, and NOT yet validated against O2 — see tools/export_geometry_cache.C.
# Commit a cache only once level 1-2 validation has passed on an O2 machine.
geometry/
